GUIDE
## Behavior units and semantic acceptance

For an interactive application, separate validation/date utilities, state persistence, DOM rendering and event wiring by their actual dependencies. Give a state-only request its API and record schema; unrelated page HTML and CSS make that responsibility harder to identify. Preserve stable IDs when rendering and wiring are separate. This is a decomposition option for work that does not complete reliably, not a requirement to split every small script.

Syntax and export checks cannot approve behavior. Exercise a valid create/change/remove/reload sequence as well as malformed records and failed writes before accepting a state module. For synchronous local storage, derive the next array, persist that candidate and update in-memory records only after the write succeeds. Saving the old array or mutating memory before persistence breaks recovery. Validate actual calendar dates, identifiers and required text rather than accepting strings that only match a regular expression.

When HTML interpolation is forbidden, specify the permitted operations concretely: replaceChildren to clear, createElement/append to construct controls, clone an existing template and assign user text through textContent. An HTML-escaping helper does not satisfy a no-innerHTML contract. Test the resulting interaction rather than accepting an absence-of-keyword check as proof.

If a diagnosed repair repeats the same defect, reduce the writable unit to one function or explicit statement slots. Preserve the raw rejected outputs and accepted neighbors. Verify semantic behavior again: a validation patch can accidentally insert an unconditional return and disable valid creation. Record host-selected boundaries, export/assembly glue and model-generated logic separately. Keep thinking settings, token limits, elapsed time and completed output as experimental evidence; a single successful narrow repair does not establish a better default or general reliability.

At a module boundary, declare parameter types, exact imported names and existing selectors. Probe a generated renderer with real typed state in the browser before passing it to the event-wiring stage. Treating an ISO date string as a Date object or inventing an external helper can propagate a bad interface into every later stage even when each file parses. A change in the accepted interface requires a new caller contract and replay, not a syntax-only checkpoint.


CONTRACT
# B2: room and rate choice

This is an assisted new-product adaptation, not exact reproduction. The primary is the actually inspected Dailyhotel reservation-flow preview in references/hotel-rooms-20261016/reference-0.jpg. The earlier Airbnb discovery reference remains authoritative for B1 search; it does not replace the hotel-room task.

## Observed anchors and chosen handoff

| ID | Observed image relationship | Implementation decision | Required comparison |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| A1 | Real return arrow above room-selection title; no promotional header | Header owns a working back control and the already supported favorite; title 객실 선택, subordinate selected property identity | Direct entry returns to browse; history returns to saved/browse context; no invented desktop/header |
| A2 | Trip/date/guest control and separate room filter occupy one functional region above cards | Actual trip editing sheet plus room-filter sheet; wrap only when necessary for text stress | Same-width header-to-control-to-first-photo sequence; open/cancel/confirm and retained draft |
| A3 | First wide photo runs flush to card top/left/right, approximately 257 by118 image pixels on296px image | Chosen aspect11/5, full card width;20px existing page inset; real separately licensed room photos | First photo remains wide/compact, not a square discovery hero or inset thumbnail |
| A4 | Room identity precedes small bed/capacity facts; price sits in subordinate quiet region | Card title18/600, facts14/500; room rates live in a quiet surface below facts; each rate has an explicit radio choice and exact money | Photo→title→facts→rate ownership stays vertical; no price/button/favorite crowding |
| A5 | Second full-width room card begins beneath first; white canvas and discreet grouping | Vertical room list;24px inter-room gap,8/12/16px internal roles; no hr/decorative bars; mobile max390 at every browser width | Compare structure/density at displayed390 and296, then enlarged text, not color or counts alone |

Original CSS, DPR, exact font family, image gallery interaction and hidden room-filter/choice behavior are unknown. The static reference does not prove any runtime. Native metadata numbers/reviews/share/gallery counters and unverified views/stock are excluded because the fictional catalogue cannot support them; exclusions cannot excuse losing these five central anchors.

## Pure dependency interface

Implement exactly export function listStayRates(catalog, stayId, trip, today, filters).
trip must be an object with exactly start,end,guests; filters exactly freeCancellation,breakfast, both booleans. start/end strings, valid explicit-today bookable range via isBookableRange; guests integer1..8; stayId nonempty string; catalog array. Invalid shape/date/today => {ok:false,error:'INVALID_ROOM_QUERY'}. Unknown valid stayId => {ok:false,error:'UNKNOWN_STAY'}.

For each room and rate of the known property in catalogue order, call accepted buildQuote(catalog,{stayId,roomId:room.id,rateId:rate.id,start:trip.start,end:trip.end,guests:trip.guests},today). Retain only successful quote results matching the requested boolean filters. Return {ok:true,quotes:[...]} including a true empty array for valid capacity/date/filter no matches. Never choose cheapest silently, mutate inputs, catch all failures as empty, use ambient time, DOM, storage or network. Imports allowed only ./dates.js and ./quote.js. No comments. Quote fields remain exactly the accepted buildQuote fields; do not add display data or copy policies.

## Connected UI scope and state

Host owns semantic markup, assembly, event boundary and fixture/photo delivery, explicitly recorded assistance. Qwen owns the bounded list dependency, quote selection behavior/rendering and scoped CSS. Do not claim fully autonomous generation from assisted output.

The current query supplies trip. Detail-specific filters start with the committed freeCancellation value and breakfast false; changing them does not overwrite discovery filters. Trip cancel/Escape leaves committed trip and selected rate unchanged. Valid trip/filter commit clears the selected rate rather than silently selecting another; validation preserves the invalid draft. Visible rate buttons are native radios in labeled fieldsets. A chosen rate must retain full property/room/rate IDs and price through the review route. Review is a separate actual view with back to room choice and retained selected quote; it shows trip, room/rate, itemized nights/cleaning/service/total and genuine inclusions. No charge/vendor confirmation, invented refund deadlines, fake progress or inert booking CTA. Local request creation remains B3/B4, not approved by this B2 scope.

Only one bottom surface is visible: navigation on B1/requests; selected-price/continue action on room selection; none on read-only review until request creation exists. Reserve actual measured bottom-surface height. Selection action stays disabled until explicit valid choice; no made-up booking button on a read-only review. Back on a fresh detail URL falls back to browse. Reload on a review URL without an in-memory selection returns to its room selection with truthful state, not a fabricated reservation.

Verify all rate identities/prices/closed nights/capacity, filter empty and recovery, trip preservation/cancel/invalid/reset, selected quote and review arithmetic, actual return routes, favorite storage faults, B1 regressions, paint ownership, official fonts/icons,296/320/390/1440,200%text and text spacing. A passed pure module or complete CSS is not reference approval. B2 still requires direct positive-anchor comparison.

ACCEPTED DEPENDENCY
import { isBookableRange } from "./dates.js";
import { selectOffers } from "./query.js";

function buildQuote(catalog, selection, today) {
    if (!Array.isArray(catalog)) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (selection === null || typeof selection !== "object" || Array.isArray(selection)) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    const keys = Object.keys(selection);
    if (keys.length !== 6) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (!keys.includes("stayId") || !keys.includes("roomId") || !keys.includes("rateId") || !keys.includes("start") || !keys.includes("end") || !keys.includes("guests")) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    const { stayId, roomId, rateId, start, end, guests } = selection;
    if (typeof stayId !== "string" || stayId === "") return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (typeof roomId !== "string" || roomId === "") return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (typeof rateId !== "string" || rateId === "") return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (typeof start !== "string" || typeof end !== "string") return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (!isBookableRange(start, end, today)) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };
    if (typeof guests !== "number" || !Number.isInteger(guests) || guests < 1 || guests > 8) return { ok: false, error: "INVALID_SELECTION" };

    let property = null;
    for (const p of catalog) {
        if (p.id === stayId) { property = p; break; }
    }
    if (!property) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    let room = null;
    for (const r of property.rooms) {
        if (r.id === roomId) { room = r; break; }
    }
    if (!room) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    if (room.capacity < guests) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    const closedDates = new Set(room.closedDates || []);
    let d = new Date(Date.UTC(
        parseInt(start.slice(0, 4), 10),
        parseInt(start.slice(5, 7), 10) - 1,
        parseInt(start.slice(8, 10), 10)
    ));
    const endDateObj = new Date(Date.UTC(
        parseInt(end.slice(0, 4), 10),
        parseInt(end.slice(5, 7), 10) - 1,
        parseInt(end.slice(8, 10), 10)
    ));

    while (d < endDateObj) {
        const y = d.getUTCFullYear();
        const m = String(d.getUTCMonth() + 1).padStart(2, "0");
        const day = String(d.getUTCDate()).padStart(2, "0");
        if (closedDates.has(`${y}-${m}-${day}`)) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };
        d.setUTCDate(d.getUTCDate() + 1);
    }

    let rate = null;
    for (const rt of room.rates) {
        if (rt.id === rateId) { rate = rt; break; }
    }
    if (!rate) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    const clonedProperty = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(property));
    const selectedRoomIndex = clonedProperty.rooms.findIndex(r => r.id === roomId);
    clonedProperty.rooms = [JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(clonedProperty.rooms[selectedRoomIndex]))];
    const selectedRateIndex = clonedProperty.rooms[0].rates.findIndex(r => r.id === rateId);
    clonedProperty.rooms[0].rates = [clonedProperty.rooms[0].rates[selectedRateIndex]];
    const singletonCatalog = [clonedProperty];
    const query = {
        city: "",
        start: start,
        end: end,
        guests: guests,
        type: "all",
        minPrice: 0,
        maxPrice: 1000000,
        freeCancellation: false,
        amenities: [],
        sort: "recommended"
    };

    const offerResult = selectOffers(singletonCatalog, query, today);
    if (!offerResult.ok || !Array.isArray(offerResult.offers)) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    let selectedOffer = null;
    for (const off of offerResult.offers) {
        if (off.roomId === roomId && off.rateId === rateId) {
            selectedOffer = off;
            break;
        }
    }

    if (!selectedOffer) return { ok: false, error: "UNAVAILABLE_SELECTION" };

    const nightly = selectedOffer.nightly;
    const nights = selectedOffer.nights;
    const cleaningFee = rate.cleaningFee;
    const serviceFee = selectedOffer.total - (nightly * nights) - cleaningFee;

    return {
        ok: true,
        quote: {
            stayId: stayId,
            roomId: roomId,
            rateId: rateId,
            start: start,
            end: end,
            guests: guests,
            nights: nights,
            nightly: nightly,
            cleaningFee: cleaningFee,
            serviceFee: serviceFee,
            total: selectedOffer.total,
            freeCancellation: rate.freeCancellation,
            breakfast: rate.breakfast,
            capacity: room.capacity
        }
    };
}

export { buildQuote };
DATE API
import {isBookableRange} from "./dates.js"; isBookableRange(start,end,today) returns boolean; accepted helper handles exact date-only strings, today, past and1..28nights. Catalogue is trusted fixture array; no need to invent additional schema. For all valid empty results use quotes:[], never fallback. Returned quote has14fields; no new fields.
